  the newest of several new messages was found and the others were never
  fetched. A SELECT or STATUS answer without UIDVALIDITY now fails the folder
  instead of reading as a changed UIDVALIDITY, which deleted every locally
  stored message of that folder. STORE, UID EXPUNGE and the COPY fallback of a
  move check the tagged status, so a server refusal is an error rather than a
  success; the fallback quotes the mailbox and runs only when MOVE was refused.
  Mailbox names are decoded without the utf7-imap crate, which panicked on a
  name that is not valid modified UTF-7. Appending a message reports the UID it
  got, looked up by its Message-ID.
